# New dining visit

When Morris names a restaurant and visit date, finish the visit in this order. Do not stop after JSON.

1. **Id** — `kebab-name-MMDDYY` from the visit date. Repeat visits get a new id.

2. **Michelin (live)** — Search the current Michelin Guide. Record `stars` 1–3 + `status` (`current`|`former`), or `rank` `gourmand`|`selected` (no `stars`), or skip Michelin. Copy cuisine/city from the listing. NYC city is `New York, NY`.

3. **Awards (cache first)** — `python3 scripts/dining-rankings.py lookup "Name"`. Check every slug in `ACCOLADE_LISTS`: 50 Best restaurants/bars (World, North America, Europe), NYT 100 Best (2023–2026, region `New York`), 101 Best burgers/steakhouses (World), 50 Top Pizza (World, North America, Europe), OAD if it appears. Cache miss or stale year → web-search the **official** list, then `python3 scripts/dining-rankings.py add ...`. Never invent a rank or a city subset.

4. **JSON** — Michelin only → `data/michelin.json`. Award only → `data/award.json` (`accolades[]` with closed-set `list` slugs). Both → **same `id`**, one photo folder. `menu` is `à la carte` | `full tasting` | `restaurant week`. `pictures` starts `[]`. Dual-listed meals share photos.

5. **Photos** — `mkdir` `components/dining/img/visits/<id>/` and open it. Stop until Morris drops files. Keep `0.jpeg`. Rename the rest `1.jpeg`, `2.jpeg`, … sorted A–Z by **original** filename. Write `pictures`, then `npm run compress-dining -- <id>`. Every listed file needs `N.jpeg` + `N.thumb.jpeg`. Do not re-compress other visits.

6. **Ship** — Commit the visit (JSON + compressed photos + thumbs only) and push to `main`.
